#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "external shopping cart basket"
msgstr "canasta externa de chango"

#. ~ Description for external shopping cart basket
#. ~ Description for external wire bike basket
#. ~ Description for external cargo rack
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Storage space, mounted outside your vehicle's armor and vulnerable to "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Sirve para almacenar cosas, va montada fuera del vehículo por lo que queda "
"vulnerable a los daños."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "folding shopping cart basket"
msgstr "canasta plegable de chango"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wire bike basket"
msgstr "canasta de alambre de bicicleta"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "external wire bike basket"
msgstr "canasta de alambre externa de bicicleta"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "box"
msgstr "caja"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "external cargo rack"
msgstr "estante externo de carga"

#. ~ Description for bike rack
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of pipes and frames for supporting a bike or other small "
"vehicle and carrying it on your vehicle.  Move a single tile wide vehicle so"
" that all of that vehicle's tiles are next to bike racks, and then 'e'xamine"
" any bike rack to mount that vehicle onto the bike rack.  'e'xamine the bike"
" rack to unmount the carried vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de caños y estructuras para sostener una bicicleta u otro "
"vehículo pequeño, y transportarlo en tu vehículo. Poné el vehículo a un "
"espacio para que queden al lado del soporte, y 'e'xaminá el soporte para "
"montar la bicicleta. También tenés que 'e'xaminá el soporte para "
"desmontarla."

#. ~ Description for mounted spare tire
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "Spare tire stored on an external carrier rig."
msgstr "Es una rueda de repuesto puesta en puerta rueda externo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A combustion engine.  Burns fuel from a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr "Es un motor de combustión. Quema combustible del tanque del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A combustion engine for use on aircraft.  Burns gasoline or avgas fuel from "
"a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es un motor de combustión para usar en aviones. Quema nafta o combustible de"
" aviación de un tanque del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A combustion engine.  Burns diesel fuel from a tank in the vehicle.  Can "
"also burn biodiesel or lamp oil, though somewhat less efficiently."
msgstr ""
"Es un motor de combustión. Quema gasoil del tanque del vehículo. También "
"puede quemar biodiésel o aceite de lámpara, aunque es menos eficiente."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A combustion engine.  Burns gasoline fuel from a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr "Es un motor de combustión. Quema nafta del tanque del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An advanced combustion engine.  Burns gasoline or diesel or aviation fuel "
"from a tank in the vehicle.  Can also burn lamp oil, though somewhat less "
"efficiently.  Better power-to-weight ratio than a traditional engine, but "
"consumes more fuel."
msgstr ""
"Es un motor avanzado de combustión. Quema nafta o gasoil o combustible de "
"aviación de un tanque del vehículo. También puede quemar aceite de lámpara, "
"aunque es menos eficiente. Es mejor en alimentación en relación a su peso "
"que un motor tradicional, pero consume más combustible."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A closed cycle, external combustion steam engine.  Burns coal or charcoal "
"from a bunker in the vehicle to produce steam."
msgstr ""
"Es un motor de vapor de combustión externa, con ciclo cerrado. Quema carbón "
"o carbón vegetal de la carbonera del vehículo para producir vapor."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "opaque door"
msgstr "puerta opaca"

#. ~ Description for opaque door
#. ~ Description for opaque wooden door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro lado cuando "
"está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy duty door"
msgstr "puerta reforzada"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strong door.  Has a window so you can see out of it, even when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Tiene una ventana para poder ver para afuera "
"aunque esté cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy duty opaque door"
msgstr "puerta opaca reforzada"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty opaque door
#. ~ Description for opaque hatch
#. ~ Description for shutter door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strong door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro "
"lado cuando está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "internal door"
msgstr "puerta interna"

#. ~ Description for internal door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An interior door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta interior. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro "
"lado cuando está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "hatch"
msgstr "escotilla"

#. ~ Description for hatch
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A strong door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando "
"está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "opaque hatch"
msgstr "escotilla opaca"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy duty hatch"
msgstr "escotilla reforzada"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty hatch
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A very strong door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta muy resistente. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando"
" está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "opaque heavy duty hatch"
msgstr "escotilla opaca reforzada"

#. ~ Description for opaque heavy duty hatch
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A very strong door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta muy resistente. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al "
"otro lado cuando está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "boom crane"
msgstr "brazo de grúa"

#. ~ Description for boom crane
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A rigid steel boom crane.  If it is in your line of sight and within two "
"tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to "
"jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Es una grúa rígida de acero. Si está a la vista y a menos de dos espacios de"
" otro vehículo, automáticamente la vas a usar si querés levantar un auto "
"para cambiarle las ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar algún componente pesado"
" como el motor que estás instalando o sacando, la grúa tiene que estar en la"
" línea de visión del lugar a donde va, y dentro de cuatro espacios de "
"distancia."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "internal boom crane"
msgstr "brazo interno de grúa"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "telescopic crane"
msgstr "grúa telescópica"

#. ~ Description for telescopic crane
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An extendable cantilever crane.  If it is in your line of sight and within "
"two tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to"
" jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Es una grúa voladiza extensible. Si está a la vista y a menos de dos "
"espacios de otro vehículo, automáticamente la vas a usar si querés levantar "
"un auto para cambiarle las ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar algún "
"componente pesado como el motor que estás instalando o sacando, la grúa "
"tiene que estar en la línea de visión del lugar a donde va, y dentro de "
"cuatro espacios de distancia."

#. ~ Description for pallet lifter
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small pallet lifter.  If it is in your line of sight and within two tiles "
"of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to jack up "
"the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy component"
" like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must have "
"line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of it."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña zorra hidráulica. Si está a la vista y a menos de dos "
"espacios de otro vehículo, automáticamente la vas a usar si querés levantar "
"un auto para cambiarle las ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar algún "
"componente pesado como el motor que estás instalando o sacando, la grúa "
"tiene que estar en la línea de visión del lugar a donde va, y dentro de "
"cuatro espacios de distancia."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "forklift arm"
msgstr "brazo de montacargas"

#. ~ Description for forklift arm
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pair of forklift arms.  If it is in your line of sight and within two "
"tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to "
"jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Es un par de brazos de montacarga. Si está a la vista y a menos de dos "
"espacios de otro vehículo, automáticamente la vas a usar si querés levantar "
"un auto para cambiarle las ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar algún "
"componente pesado como el motor que estás instalando o sacando, la grúa "
"tiene que estar en la línea de visión del lugar a donde va, y dentro de "
"cuatro espacios de distancia."

#. ~ Description for rockwheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large metal disc, powered by the vehicle's engines.  Use the vehicle "
"controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it will stop the vehicle "
"unless it has a strong engine.  When turned on, it will dig a shallow pit in"
" dirt.  Mount it on the edge of your vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es un disco grande metálico, alimentado por los motores del vehículo. Usá "
"los controles del vehículo para activarla o desactivarla. Cuando está "
"activada, hará que el vehículo se detenga a menos que tenga un motor fuerte."
" Cuando está encendido, cavará un pozo poco profundo en la tierra. Hay que "
"instalarlo en el costado del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "air jack system"
msgstr "sistema de gato de aire"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "foldable light frame"
msgstr "armazón liviana plegable"

#. ~ Description for foldable light frame
#. ~ Description for foldable orichalcum frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light metal framework, designed to fold.  Other vehicle components can be "
"mounted on it.  If all the frames and components of a vehicle are foldable, "
"the vehicle can be folding into a small package and picked up as a normal "
"item."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura ligera de metal, diseñada para plegarse. Se pueden poner "
"otras partes del vehículo en ella. Si todas las estructuras y componentes de"
" un vehículo son plegables, el vehículo puede ser plegado en un pequeño "
"paquete y llevado como un objeto normal."

#. ~ Description for foldable wooden frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light wooden framework, designed to fold.  Other vehicle components can be"
" mounted on it.  If all the frames and components of a vehicle are foldable,"
" the vehicle can be folding into a small package and picked up as a normal "
"item."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura ligera de madera, diseñada para plegarse. Se pueden poner "
"otras partes del vehículo en ella. Si todas las estructuras y componentes de"
" un vehículo son plegables, el vehículo puede ser plegado en un pequeño "
"paquete y llevado como un objeto normal."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "frame"
msgstr "armazón"

#. ~ Description for frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and it "
"can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura de metal. Se pueden poner otras partes del vehículo en "
"ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el tamaño del "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description for wooden frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wooden framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and it "
"can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  Wood and "
"nail construction means it can be constructed and added to the vehicle "
"without welding tools."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura de madera. Se pueden poner otras partes del vehículo en "
"ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el tamaño del "
"vehículo. La construcción hecha con maderas y clavos significa que podés "
"seguir agrandando el vehículo sin la necesidad de herramientas para soldar."

#. ~ Description for light wooden frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light wooden framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, "
"and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  Wood"
" and rope constructions means it can be constructed and added to the vehicle"
" without welding tools or nails."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura ligera de madera. Se pueden poner otras partes del "
"vehículo en ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el "
"tamaño del vehículo. La construcción hecha con maderas y sogas significa que"
" podés seguir agrandando el vehículo sin la necesidad de herramientas para "
"soldar o clavos."

#. ~ Description for heavy duty frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A heavy metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and"
" it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  "
"Increased mass makes it more resistant to damage in collisions."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura de metal resistente. Se pueden poner otras partes del "
"vehículo en ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el "
"tamaño del vehículo. Al incrementar la masa se vuelve más resistente al daño"
" durante las colisiones."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "extra light frame"
msgstr "armazón extra-liviana"

#. ~ Description for extra light frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and"
" it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura ligera de metal. Se pueden poner otras partes del vehículo"
" en ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el tamaño "
"del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "aisle lights"
msgstr "luces de pasillo"

#. ~ Description for atomic lamp
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bright light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops.  "
"When turned on, it illuminates several squares inside the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante, autoalimentada por una reacción atómica radioactiva "
"que nunca para. Cuando está encendida, ilumina varios espacios adentro del "
"vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "atomic nightlight"
msgstr "velador atómico"

#. ~ Description for atomic nightlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A very dim light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops."
"  When turned on, it illuminates a single square inside the vehicle that "
"isn't suitable for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz muy suave, autoalimentada por una reacción atómica radiactiva que"
" nunca para. Cuando está encendida, ilumina un solo espacio adentro del "
"vehículo y no es adecuada para trabajar."

#. ~ Description for floodlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A very bright, circular light that illuminates the area outside the vehicle "
"when turned on."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz circular muy brillante, que ilumina el área exterior del vehículo"
" cuando está encendida."

#. ~ Description for directed floodlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A very bright, directed light that illuminates a half-circular area outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz muy brillante dirigible que ilumina un área semicircular en el "
"exterior del vehículo cuando está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés "
"elegir la dirección en la que apuntará."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "headlight"
msgstr "luz delantera"

#. ~ Description for headlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside the vehicle when "
"turned on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the "
"light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as "
"the front."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante que ilumina un cono angosto afuera del vehículo cuando "
"está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés elegir la dirección en la que "
"apuntará, así que con varias luces delanteras podés iluminar los costados y "
"la parte posterior tan bien como la delantera."

#. ~ Description for motorcycle headlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small, lightweight, bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the "
"sides or rear, as well as the front."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante pequeña y liviana que ilumina un cono angosto afuera "
"del vehículo cuando está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés elegir la "
"dirección en la que apuntará, así que con varias luces delanteras podés "
"iluminar los costados y la parte posterior tan bien como la delantera."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wide angle headlight"
msgstr "luz delantera amplia"

#. ~ Description for wide angle headlight
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a wide cone outside the vehicle when turned "
"on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the light, "
"so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as the "
"front."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante que ilumina un cono ancho afuera del vehículo cuando "
"está encendida. Durante su instalación, podés elegir la dirección en la que "
"apuntará, así que con varias luces delanteras podés iluminar los costados y "
"la parte posterior tan bien como la delantera."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Emergency lights, like a police car's or ambulance's, mounted on the "
"vehicle's roof.  Flashes between red and blue when turned on, attracting "
"attention without illuminating the area."
msgstr ""
"Son luces de emergencia, como las de una patrulla o una ambulancia, puestas "
"en el techo del vehículo. Destellan entre el rojo y el azul cuando están "
"encendidas, atrayendo la atención sin iluminar el área."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "blue light"
msgstr "luz azul"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "red light"
msgstr "luz roja"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "aisle with lights"
msgstr "pasillo con luces"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "foot pedals"
msgstr "pedales de pie"

#. ~ Description for foot pedals
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of bicycle style foot pedals.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, "
"they allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de pedales como los de una bicicleta. Si están puestos en el "
"mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu "
"esfuerzo (resistencia)."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "hand rims"
msgstr "aros de ruedas"

#. ~ Description for hand rims
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of wheelchair style wheels.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, they"
" allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de ruedas como los de una silla de rueda. Si están puestos en"
" el mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu "
"esfuerzo (resistencia)."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wing mirror"
msgstr "espejo lateral"

#. ~ Description for wing mirror
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted outside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño espejo, puesto fuera del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu visión"
" estará incrementada como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "inboard mirror"
msgstr "espejo retrovisor"

#. ~ Description for inboard mirror
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted inside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño espejo, puesto dentro del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu "
"visión estará incrementada como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#. ~ Description for electric motor
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "An electric motor."
msgstr "Es un motor eléctrico."

#. ~ Description for quantum solar panel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An extremely high performance solar panel.  Will recharge the vehicle's "
"electrical power when exposed to the sun.  Clouds will slow the recharge "
"speed.  Extremely fragile and cannot be armored."
msgstr ""
"Es un panel solar de muy alto rendimiento. Cargará lentamente la energía "
"eléctrica del vehículo cuando está expuesto al sol. Las nubes harán más "
"lenta la recarga. Extremadamente frágil y no puede blindarse."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Cerberus laser cannon"
msgstr "cañón láser Cerberus montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A reinforced ram.  Place at the edge of vehicle to reduce damage taken in "
"collisions, and to increase damaged delivered in collisions, if the ram is "
"the first vehicle part to collide."
msgstr ""
"Es un ariete reforzado. Ponelo en el borde del vehículo para reducir el daño"
" recibido durante las colisiones, y para incrementar el daño causado, si es "
"que el ariete es la primera parte del vehículo que choca."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "superalloy ram"
msgstr "ariete de superaleación"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero pesado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "military composite ram"
msgstr "ariete de compuesto militar"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "spiked ram"
msgstr "ariete con púas"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden ram"
msgstr "ariete de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "chitin ram"
msgstr "ariete de quitina"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "biosilicified chitin ram"
msgstr "ariete de quitina biosilicificada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "tied mattress"
msgstr "colchón atado"

#. ~ Description for tied mattress
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A mattress, strapped onto the vehicle.  It could serve to blunt any impact."
msgstr ""
"Es un colchón atado a un vehículo. Puede servir para reducir los impactos."

#. ~ Description for shredder
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A circular blade, powered by the vehicle's engine.  It will dramatically "
"increase the damage the vehicle delivers in collisions.  Mount on the edges "
"of the vehicle, preferably the front."
msgstr ""
"Es una sierra circular, alimentada con la energía del vehículo. Incrementará"
" dramáticamente el daño causado durante una colisión. Ponelo en los bordes "
"del vehículo, preferiblemente adelante."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of aerofoil helicopter rotors, when spun at high speed, they generate "
"thrust via lift."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de alerones rotores de helicóptero, que cuando giran a gran "
"velocidad generan un empuje elevador."

#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military rotors
#. ~ Description for small helicopter rotors
#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of four military-grade helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift "
"by rotation."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de cuatro aspas rotoras de helicóptero militar usadas para "
"brindar elevación por rotación."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "small helicopter rotors"
msgstr "rotores pequeños de helicóptero"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors"
msgstr "rotores militares de Blackhawk"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy-duty military Osprey rotors"
msgstr "rotores militares de Osprey"

#. ~ Description for heavy-duty military Osprey rotors
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of three military-grade helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift "
"by rotation."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de tres aspas rotoras de helicóptero militar usadas para "
"brindar elevación por rotación."

#. ~ Description for seat
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A place to sit, or sleep if you're desperate."
msgstr "Es un lugar para sentarse, o para dormir si estás medio desesperado."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "reclining seat"
msgstr "asiento reclinable"

#. ~ Description for reclining seat
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A place to sit, and the backrest reclines to make it an uncomfortable bed."
msgstr ""
"Es un lugar para sentarse, cuyo respaldo se reclina para convertirlo en una "
"cama incómoda."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "reclining leather seat"
msgstr "asiento reclinable de cuero"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "back seat"
msgstr "asiento de atrás"

#. ~ Description for back seat
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A benchlike seat.  Mostly found in the second row, also known as the back or"
" rear seat."
msgstr ""
"Es un asiento parecido a un banco. Está comúnmente en las segundas filas, "
"también se lo conoce como asiento de atrás o trasero."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "leather back seat"
msgstr "asiento de atrás de cuero"

#. ~ Description for saddle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A padded wedge that you straddle, like a bicycle or motorcycle."
msgstr ""
"Es una cuña acolchada en la cual te podés sentar, como en una moto o "
"bicicleta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "foldable seat"
msgstr "asiento plegable"

#. ~ Description for foldable seat
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A crude seat, too uncomfortable to sleep in."
msgstr "Es un asiento rudimentario, demasiado incómodo para dormir encima."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle tank (2L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (2L)"

#. ~ Description for vehicle tank (2L)
#. ~ Description for vehicle tank (10L)
#. ~ Description for vehicle tank (20L)
#. ~ Description for vehicle tank (60L)
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids.  If filled with the appropriate fuel "
"for the vehicle's engine, the engine will automatically draw fuel from the "
"tank when the engine is on.  If filled with water, you can access the water "
"from a water faucet, if one is installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a"
" rubber hose to siphon liquids out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de almacenamiento para líquidos. Si se lo llena con el "
"combustible apropiado para el motor del vehículo, el motor lo usará "
"automáticamente cuando está encendido. Si está lleno de agua, podés acceder "
"a ella por la canilla, si es que hay una instalada en el vehículo. También "
"podés usar una manguera de goma para chupar el líquido del tanque."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle tank (10L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (10L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle tank (20L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (20L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle tank (60L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (60L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "refrigerated tank (60L)"
msgstr "tanque refrigerado (60L)"

#. ~ Description for refrigerated tank (60L)
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A 60L refrigerated tank.  When turned on, it will cool the liquid inside, "
"extending the time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Es un tanque refrigerado de 60 litros. Cuando está encendido enfriará el "
"líquido que contenga, extendiendo el tiempo de duración de los alimentos."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "external tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque externo (100L)"

#. ~ Description for external tank (100L)
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted outside the vehicle's walls and"
" armor.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If"
" filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de almacenamiento para líquidos, puesto fuera del vehículo y "
"su protección. Si se lo llena con el combustible apropiado para el motor del"
" vehículo, el motor lo usará automáticamente cuando está encendido. Si está "
"lleno de agua, podés acceder a ella por la canilla, si es que hay una "
"instalada en el vehículo. También podés usar una manguera de goma para "
"chupar el líquido del tanque."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado en techo (100L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "external tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo (200L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado en techo (200L)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden barrel (100L)"
msgstr "barril de madera (100L)"

#. ~ Description for wooden barrel (100L)
#. ~ Description for steel drum (100L)
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted inside the cargo or passenger "
"space.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If"
" filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de almacenamiento para líquidos, puesto dentro en el espacio "
"para carga o en el lugar del acompañante. Si se lo llena con el combustible "
"apropiado para el motor del vehículo, el motor lo usará automáticamente "
"cuando está encendido. Si está lleno de agua, podés acceder a ella por la "
"canilla, si es que hay una instalada en el vehículo. También podés usar una "
"manguera de goma para chupar el líquido del tanque."

#. ~ Description for fuel bunker
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding solid fuels.  If filled with the appropriate "
"fuel for the vehicle's engine, the engine will automatically draw fuel from "
"the tank when the engine is on."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de almacenamiento para combustible sólido. Si se lo llena con "
"el combustible apropiado para el motor del vehículo, el motor lo usará "
"automáticamente cuando está encendido."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted makeshift chemical thrower"
msgstr "lanzador químico improvisado montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted XM34 EMP projector"
msgstr "proyector XM34 PEM montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted H&K G80 Railgun"
msgstr "cañón de riel H&K G80 montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted flamethrower"
msgstr "lanzallamas montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted PPA-5 plasma gun"
msgstr "pistola de plasma PPA-5 montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted A7 laser rifle"
msgstr "rifle láser A7 montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M249"
msgstr "M249 montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M249S"
msgstr "M249S montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted gatling shotgun"
msgstr "escopeta gatling montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M2 Browning"
msgstr "M2 Browning montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M134D-H Minigun"
msgstr "Minigun M134D-H montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgstr "Rifle Automático Browning montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M240"
msgstr "M240 montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M60"
msgstr "M60 montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr "M60 Semi Auto montada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Mark 19 grenade launcher"
msgstr "lanzagranadas Mark 19 montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted BGM-71F TOW"
msgstr "BGM-71F TOW montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted RM298 HMG"
msgstr "RM298 HMG montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted RM614 LMG"
msgstr "RM614 LMG montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Boeing XM-P plasma rifle"
msgstr "rilfe de plasma Boeing XM-P montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted coilgun"
msgstr "cañón Gauss montado"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "plugged 3-inch ordnance rifle"
msgstr "rifle de 3 pulgadas ordnance obstruido"

#. ~ Description for plugged 3-inch ordnance rifle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, some responsible killjoy poured concrete in the barrel of "
"this historic cannon to make it safe for display."
msgstr ""
"Lamentablemente, algún aguafiestas le puso concreto en el cañón de esta "
"histórica arma para hacerla más segura durante las representaciones."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "kitchen unit"
msgstr "cocina"

#. ~ Description for kitchen unit
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small but complete kitchen unit, powered from the vehicle's batteries."
msgstr ""
"Es una unidad de cocina pequeña pero completa, alimentada por las baterías "
"del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "welding rig"
msgstr "equipo soldador"

#. ~ Description for welding rig
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A welding rig mounted in the vehicle, that draws power from the vehicle's "
"batteries.  You still need glare protection.  'e'xamine the tile with the "
"rig to use it to repair items in your inventory.  If you attempt to craft an"
" item or perform a repair that requires a welder, you will be given the "
"option of using the welding rig."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo soldador montado en un vehículo que utiliza la energía de las "
"baterías. Necesitás protección para los ojos. Con 'e' examinás el lugar "
"donde está la soldadora para usarla para reparar objetos en tu inventario. "
"Si intentás fabricar un objeto o hacer una reparación que necesita una "
"soldadora, vas a tener la opción de utilizar este equipo."

#. ~ Description for FOODCO kitchen buddy
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A multi-function crafting station, with a water purifier, food dehydrator, "
"vacuum sealer, and hand press for making ammo.  Draws power from the "
"vehicle's batteries.  'e'xamine the tile with the kitchen buddy to access "
"the water faucet or to purify water in a vehicle tank or in a container in "
"your inventory.  If you attempt to craft an item that needs one of the "
"kitchen buddy's functions, it will automatically be selected as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Es una estación de fabricación multifunción, con un purificador de agua, un "
"deshidratador de comida, un sellador al vacío y una prensa de mano para "
"fabricar munición. Utiliza la energía de las baterías del vehículo. Usá 'e' "
"para examinar el lugar con la cocina amistosa para acceder a la canilla o "
"para purificar agua en un tanque del vehículo, o en un recipiente en tu "
"inventario. Si intentás fabricar un objeto que necesita una de las funciones"
" de la cocina amistosa, automáticamente será seleccionada como herramienta."

#. ~ Description for onboard chemistry lab
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small chemistry station, including a hotplate and electrolysis setup "
"powered by the vehicle's batteries.  'e'xamine the tile with the chemistry "
"lab to access the water faucet or to heat up food with the hotplate.  If you"
" attempt to craft an item that needs one of the chemistry lab's functions, "
"it will automatically be selected as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo pequeño de química, que incluye un anafe y un equipo de "
"electrólisis alimentado por las baterías del vehículo. Usá 'e' para examinar"
" el lugar con el equipo de química para acceder a la canilla o para calentar"
" comida en el anafe. Si intentás fabricar un objeto que necesita una de las "
"funciones del equipo de química, automáticamente será seleccionado como "
"herramienta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted electric forge"
msgstr "forja eléctrica montada"

#. ~ Description for mounted electric forge
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A electric forge for metalworking, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  With"
" a hammer and other tools, you could use this for metalworking.  If you "
"attempt to craft an item that needs a forge, you will be given the option of"
" selecting it as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Es una forja eléctrica para trabajar con metal, alimentada por las baterías "
"del vehículo. Con un martillo y otras herramientas, podrías usarla para "
"trabajos de herrería. Si intentás fabricar un objeto que necesita una forja,"
" tendrás la opción de utilizarla como herramienta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted electric kiln"
msgstr "fosa de carbonización eléctrica montada"

#. ~ Description for mounted electric kiln
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A electric kiln for baking brick or clay, powered by the vehicle's "
"batteries.  You could use this to harden bricks or clay.  If you attempt to "
"craft an item that needs a kiln, you will be given the option of selecting "
"it as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Es una fosa de carbonización eléctrica para cocinar ladrillos o arcilla, "
"alimentada por las baterías del vehículo. Podés usarla para endurecer los "
"ladrillos o la arcilla. Si intentás fabricar un objeto que necesita una fosa"
" de carbonización, tendrás la opción de utilizarla como herramienta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "null part"
msgstr "parte no válida"

#. ~ Description for yoke and harness
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Attach this part to a beast of burden to allow it to pull your vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Ponele esto a una bestia de carga para permitirle tirar de tu vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cart handle"
msgstr "manija de carro"

#. ~ Description for cart handle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A metal handle, a creature with hands could use it to push a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una manija de metal que una criatura con manos puede usar para empujar un"
" vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "tracking device"
msgstr "dispositivo de rastreo"

#. ~ Description for tracking device
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A small transmitter that lets you locate the vehicle on the map."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño transmisor que te permite localizar vehículos en el mapa."

#. ~ Description for bed
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A small but comfortable bed."
msgstr "Es una cama chica pero cómoda."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "handle"
msgstr "manija"

#. ~ Description for handle
#. ~ Description for wooden handle
#. ~ Description for light wooden handle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A pair of handles.  You can mount other items on top of it."
msgstr "Es un manubrio. Le podés agregar otros objetos encima."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden handle"
msgstr "manija de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "light wooden handle"
msgstr "manija ligera de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "aisle"
msgstr "pasillo"

#. ~ Description for aisle
#. ~ Description for wooden aisle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "An aisle."
msgstr "Es un pasillo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden aisle"
msgstr "pasillo de madera"

#. ~ Description for floor trunk
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "An aisle.  A hatch lets you access a cargo space beneath it."
msgstr ""
"Es un pasillo. Una escotilla te permite acceder al espacio de almacenamiento"
" que hay debajo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cloth roof"
msgstr "techo de tela"

#. ~ Description for cloth roof
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A cloth roof."
msgstr "Es un techo de tela."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "roof"
msgstr "techo"

#. ~ Description for roof
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A metal roof."
msgstr "Es un techo de metal."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy duty roof"
msgstr "techo reforzado"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty roof
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A thick metal roof."
msgstr "Es un techo de metal grueso."

#. ~ Description for blade
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A blade, welded to the vehicle, for cutting up zombies."
msgstr "Es una cuchilla soldada al vehículo... para cortar zombis."

#. ~ Description for spike
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A metal spike, welded to the vehicle, to increase injury when crashing into "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Es una púa de metal soldada al vehículo, para incrementar el daño causado "
"cuando choca contra algo."

#. ~ Description for programmable autopilot
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A computer system hooked up to the steering and engine of the vehicle to "
"allow it to follow simple paths."
msgstr ""
"Es un sistema computarizado conectado a la dirección y al motor del vehículo"
" para permitirle realizar caminos simples."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "swappable storage battery case"
msgstr "caja para batería de alm. cambiable"

#. ~ Description for swappable storage battery case
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A battery case for storage batteries.  Allows quick removal or addition of a"
" storage battery, if you can lift the battery."
msgstr ""
"Es una caja para baterías de almacenamiento. Permite sacar o poner "
"rápidamente una batería, si podés levantarla la batería..."

#. ~ Description for military black box
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An armored black box, a device meant to record and preserve data of a "
"military vehicle in the field in case it gets destroyed."
msgstr ""
"Es una caja negra blindada, un dispositivo pensado para grabar y preservar "
"la información de un vehículo militar en el campo, en caso de que sea "
"destruido."

#. ~ Description for minireactor
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small nuclear reactor.  When loaded with plutonium cells and turned on, "
"will generate a lot of electrical power."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño reactor nuclear. Cuando está cargado con celdas de plutonio y "
"es encendido, generará mucha energía eléctrica."

#. ~ Description for minifridge
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small fridge.  When turned on, it will cool the food inside, extended the "
"time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña heladera. Cuando está encendida enfriará la comida que tenga "
"adentro, extendiendo el tiempo de duración de los alimentos."

#. ~ Description for washing machine
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small washing machine.  With detergent, water, and some electrical power, "
"you could clean a lot of clothes.  'e'xamine the tile with the washing "
"machine to use it."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño lavarropas. Con detergente, agua y energía eléctrica, podría "
"lavar mucha ropa. Apretá 'e' para examinarlo y usarlo."

#. ~ Description for dishwasher
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small dishwasher.  With detergent, water, and some electrical power, you "
"could clean your dishes…  Or something more useful like a CBM dripping with "
"zombie gore.  'e'xamine the tile with the dishwasher to use it."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño lavavajillas. Con detergente, agua y energía eléctrica, "
"podrías lavar los platos… O algo más útil como un MCB que está chorreando "
"con los restos de un zombi. Apretá 'e' para examinarlo y usarlo."

#. ~ Description for autoclave
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is an autoclave.  It's useful for sterilizing things like CBMs.  "
"'e'xamine the tile with the autoclave to use it."
msgstr ""
"Esto es un autoclave. Es útil para esterilizar cosas como los MCB. Apretá "
"'e' para examinarlo y usarlo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "trunk"
msgstr "baúl"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "travois"
msgstr "narria"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wood box"
msgstr "caja de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "folding wood box"
msgstr "caja plegable de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wood table"
msgstr "mesa de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden boat hull"
msgstr "casco de madera de bote"

#. ~ Description for wooden boat hull
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A wooden board that keeps the water out of your boat."
msgstr "Es una tabla de madera que mantiene el agua afuera de tu bote."

#. ~ Description for raft boat hull
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "Logs tied together that will keep your boat out of the water."
msgstr "Son troncos atados juntos que van a mantener tu bote flotando."

#. ~ Description for plastic boat hull
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A rigid plastic sheet that keeps water out of your boat."
msgstr ""
"Es una lámina rígida de plástico que mantiene el agua afuera de tu bote."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "metal boat hull"
msgstr "casco de metal de bote"

#. ~ Description for metal boat hull
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A metal sheet that keeps the water out of your boat."
msgstr "Es una plancha de metal que mantiene el agua afuera de tu bote."

#. ~ Description for carbon fiber boat hull
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A light weight, advanced carbon fiber rigid sheet that keeps the water out "
"of your boat."
msgstr ""
"Es una lámina rígida y liviana de fibra de carbono que mantiene el agua "
"afuera de tu bote."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "hand paddles"
msgstr "paletas de mano"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "reins and tackle"
msgstr "riendas y aparejo"

#. ~ Description for reins and tackle
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of leather bindings to control a creature pulling a vehicle, such as a"
" cart."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de ataduras de cuero que se usan para controlar una criatura "
"que está tirando de un vehículo como puede ser un carro."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "controls"
msgstr "controles"

#. ~ Description for controls
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A steering wheel and accelerator and brake pedals."
msgstr "Es un volante y pedales para acelerar y frenar."

#. ~ Description for dashboard
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A frame containing some lights and controls."
msgstr "Es una estructura que contiene controles y luces."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle-mounted heater"
msgstr "calentador montado en vehículo"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "vehicle-mounted cooler"
msgstr "refrigerador montado en vehículo"

#. ~ Description for electronics control unit
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "Some switches and knobs to control the vehicle's electrical systems."
msgstr ""
"Son unos interruptores y perillas para control los sistemas eléctricos del "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description for muffler
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A metal pipe that somewhat reduces engine noise."
msgstr "Es un caño de metal que reduce un poco el ruido del motor."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "seatbelt"
msgstr "cinturón de seguridad"

#. ~ Description for seatbelt
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A belt, attached to a seat."
msgstr "Es un cinturón unido al asiento."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "security system"
msgstr "sistema de seguridad"

#. ~ Description for security system
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A bunch of electronics that make it difficult to start the vehicle without "
"the proper key, and that will sound an alarm if you try.  The alarm can be "
"disabled."
msgstr ""
"Son dispositivos electrónicos que dificultan el encendido del motor sin la "
"llave adecuada, y que harán sonar una alarma si lo intentás. La alarma puede"
" ser desactivada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "smart engine controller"
msgstr "controlador inteligente de motor"

#. ~ Description for smart engine controller
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Electronic module that automatically switches combustion and electric "
"engines on and off minimizing fuel consumption and optimizing power output "
"and battery charge rate.  Must be turned on to work.  Simplified ruleset: 1."
" When throttling, maximize acceleration.  2. Keep battery at 90%.  3. "
"Minimize fuel consumption."
msgstr ""
"Es un módulo electrónico que cambia automáticamente entre los motores de "
"combustión y eléctricos para minimizar el consumo de combustible y optimizar"
" la utilización de energía y la carga de la batería. Debe estar encendido "
"para trabajar. Regla simplificada: 1. Cuando se acelera, se maximiza la "
"aceleración. 2. Mantener batería al 90%. 3. Minimizar el consumo de "
"combustible."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "5-point harness"
msgstr "arnés de 5 puntos"

#. ~ Description for 5-point harness
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A series of straps attached to the seat, intended to fasten together after "
"going over your shoulders and hips and between your legs."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de correas unidas al asiento, diseñadas para ajustarse "
"pasando por arriba de los hombros y caderas, y entre las piernas."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "curtain"
msgstr "cortina"

#. ~ Description for curtain
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A sheet over a window."
msgstr "Es una cortina sobre una ventana."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "aisle curtain"
msgstr "cortina de pasillo"

#. ~ Description for aisle curtain
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A sheet across an aisle."
msgstr "Es una cortina sobre un pasillo."

#. ~ Description for water wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A water wheel."
msgstr "Es una rueda hidráulica."

#. ~ Description for large water wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A large water wheel with wooden supports."
msgstr "Es una rueda hidráulica grande con soportes de madera."

#. ~ Description for solar panel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A solar panel."
msgstr "Es un panel solar."

#. ~ Description for wind turbine
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A small wind turbine."
msgstr "Es una turbina de viento chica."

#. ~ Description for large wind turbine
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large wind turbine with stabilizing legs.  Will cause extra drag on the "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una turbina de viento grande con patas para estabilizarla. Causará un "
"arrastre mayor en el vehículo."

#. ~ Description for reinforced solar panel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A solar panel.  Reinforced with armored glass to make it more resistant to "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Es un panel solar. Reforzado con vidrio blindado para hacerlo más resistente"
" al daño."

#. ~ Description for upgraded solar panel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A high performance solar panel."
msgstr "Es un panel solar de alto rendimiento."

#. ~ Description for upgraded reinforced solar panel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A high performance solar panel.  Reinforced with armored glass to make it "
"more resistant to damage."
msgstr ""
"Es un panel solar de alto rendimiento. Reforzado con vidrio blindado para "
"hacerlo más resistente al daño."

#. ~ Description for water faucet
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A water faucet."
msgstr "Es una canilla."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden armor"
msgstr "blindaje de madera"

#. ~ Description for spiked plating
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A spiked plate that will increase the damage delivered to someone else in "
"collisions."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa dentada que incrementará el daño causado en las colisiones."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "military composite armor plating"
msgstr "chapas blindadas de compuesto militar"

#. ~ Description for bicycle horn
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option to make "
"noise."
msgstr ""
"Es una bocina pequeña. Usá los controles del vehículo para seleccionar la "
"bocina y hacerla sonar."

#. ~ Description for car horn
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option to make noise."
msgstr ""
"Es una bocina. Usá los controles del vehículo para seleccionar la bocina y "
"hacerla sonar."

#. ~ Description for truck horn
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A powerful truck horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option "
"to make noise."
msgstr ""
"Es una potente bocina de camión. Usá los controles del vehículo para "
"seleccionar la bocina y hacerla sonar."

#. ~ Description for back-up beeper
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An electronic noise maker.  It will automatically make noise when you drive "
"in reverse, alerting things behind you to move out of the way."
msgstr ""
"Es un creador de ruido electrónico. Automáticamente, hará sonar un pitido "
"cuando manejes marcha atrás, alertando a las cosas detrás tuyo para que se "
"corran."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "trunk door"
msgstr "puerta de baúl"

#. ~ Description for trunk door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A short door.  You can always see over it, open or closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta corta. Siempre podés ver por arriba de ella, ya sea que esté "
"cerrada o abierta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy duty trunk door"
msgstr "puerta de baúl reforzada"

#. ~ Description for heavy duty trunk door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A strong, short door.  You can always see over it, open or closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una potente puerta corta. Siempre podés ver por arriba de ella, ya sea "
"que esté cerrada o abierta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "shutter door"
msgstr "puerta de persiana"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "sliding door"
msgstr "puerta corrediza"

#. ~ Description for sliding door
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando está cerrada."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cargo space"
msgstr "espacio de carga"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "livestock stall"
msgstr "casilla de ganado"

#. ~ Description for livestock stall
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cargo space for carrying livestock.  'e'xamine it to capture an animal "
"next to you, or to release the animal currently contained.  When selecting "
"an animal to capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the part."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de carga para llevar ganado. Usá 'e' para examinar y capturar "
"un animal cercano, o para liberar al animal que esté adentro. Cuando "
"selecciones el animal para capturar, seleccioná el espacio en el que está en"
" relación a vos, no a la parte."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "animal compartment"
msgstr "compartimiento animal"

#. ~ Description for animal compartment
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large locker for transporting smaller animals.  'e'xamine it to capture an"
" animal next to you, or to release the animal currently contained.  When "
"selecting an animal to capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the "
"part."
msgstr ""
"Es un casillero grande para transportar animales pequeños. Usá 'e' para "
"examinar y capturar un animal cercano, o para liberar al animal que esté "
"adentro. Cuando selecciones el animal para capturar, seleccioná el espacio "
"en el que está en relación a vos, no a la parte."

#. ~ Description for recharging station
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A device for recharging batteries.  When turned on, it charges any "
"rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc) placed "
"directly in the attached storage space."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo para recargar baterías. Cuando está encendido, carga "
"cualquier batería recargable (de celdas, de plomo y ácido, etc.) que estén "
"puestas directamente en el espacio de almacenamiento."

#. ~ Description for battery charger
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small, low-power consumer device for recharging batteries.  It slowly "
"charges any rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc)"
" placed directly in the attached storage space."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo pequeño de bajo consumo para recargar baterías. Carga "
"lentamente cualquier batería recargable (de celdas, de plomo y ácido, etc.) "
"que estén puestas directamente en el espacio de almacenamiento."

#. ~ Description for stereo system
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A stereo system.  When turned on, it plays music, improving your mood."
msgstr ""
"Es un sistema estéreo. Cuando está encendido reproduce música, mejorando tu "
"humor."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "chimes"
msgstr "campanas"

#. ~ Description for chimes
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A collection of electronic bells.  Use the vehicle's controls to turn it on "
"or off.  When turned on, it makes noise, attracting neighborhood children."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de campanas electrónicas. Usá los controles del vehículo para"
" encenderlo o apagarlo. Cuando está encendido, hace ruido, atrayendo a los "
"niños del barrio."

#. ~ Description for jumper cable
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one vehicle "
"and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power between the "
"two."
msgstr ""
"Es un cable grueso de cobre con conductores en las dos puntas. Poné una "
"punta en un vehículo y la otra en otro, y podés transferir energía eléctrica"
" entre los vehículos."

#. ~ Description for heavy-duty cable
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Very thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one "
"vehicle and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power "
"between the two."
msgstr ""
"Es un cable muy grueso de cobre con conductores en las dos puntas. Poné una "
"punta en un vehículo y la otra en otro, y podés transferir energía eléctrica"
" entre los vehículos."

#. ~ Description for heavy duty tow cable
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A heavy duty tow cable, if the other end was attached to another vehicle, it"
" could pull it."
msgstr ""
"Es un cable reforzado para remolcar. Si la otra punta está enganchada a otro"
" vehículo podría remolcarlo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "flimsy wooden seat"
msgstr "asiento endeble de madera"

#. ~ Description for flimsy wooden seat
#. ~ Description for wooden seat
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A place to sit."
msgstr "Es un lugar para sentarse."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden seat"
msgstr "asiento de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden bench"
msgstr "banco de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden bench
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A benchlike place to sit."
msgstr "Es un banco para sentarse."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden spike"
msgstr "púa de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden spike
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wooden spike, attached to the vehicle, to increase injury when crashing "
"into things."
msgstr ""
"Es una púa de madera unida al vehículo, para incrementar el daño causado "
"cuando choca contra algo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden door"
msgstr "puerta de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "opaque wooden door"
msgstr "puerta opaca de madera"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden roof"
msgstr "techo de madera"

#. ~ Description for wooden roof
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A wooden roof."
msgstr "Es un techo de madera."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "chitin plating"
msgstr "chapas de quitina"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "biosilicified chitin plating"
msgstr "chapas de quitina biosilicificada"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "door motor"
msgstr "puerta de motor"

#. ~ Description for door motor
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small electric motor.  Installed on the same frame as a door or curtain, "
"it will allow you to remotely open the door or curtain from the vehicle "
"controls."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño motor eléctrico. Instalado en la misma estructura que una "
"puerta o cortina, te permite controlar su apertura de manera remota desde "
"los controles del vehículo."

#. ~ Description for drive by wire controls
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sophisticated set of electronic controls that allow you to control the "
"vehicle from a vehicle remote while you are not in it.  You can 'e'xamine "
"the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control key (default "
"'^')."
msgstr ""
"Es un sofisticado equipo de controles electrónicos que te permiten manejar "
"el vehículo de manera remota. Podés 'e'xaminar el espacio para acceder a los"
" controles, o usar la tecla de control del vehículo (por defecto '^')."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "camera control system"
msgstr "sistema de cámara de control"

#. ~ Description for camera control system
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An LCD attached to one or more cameras.  When turned on, it lets you see "
"from the cameras, but drains power from the vehicle's batteries.  You can "
"'e'xamine the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control key "
"(default '^')."
msgstr ""
"Es un LCD conectado a una o más cámaras. Cuando está encendido, te permite "
"ver las cámaras pero consume energía de las baterías del vehículo. Podés "
"'e'xaminar el espacio para acceder a los controles, o usar la tecla de "
"control del vehículo (por defecto '^')."

#. ~ Description for security camera
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A small camera.  Will relay what it can see to a camera control station."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña cámara. Transmite lo que ve a la estación de control de "
"cámaras."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "robot controls"
msgstr "controles de robot"

#. ~ Description for robot controls
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of controls to allow a vehicle to drive itself, or you to drive it "
"remotely using a controller."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo de controles que permiten que el vehículo se maneje solo, o que"
" puedas manejarlo remotamente con un control."

#. ~ Description for clock
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A clock, so you know what time it is."
msgstr "Es un reloj, así podés saber la hora."

#. ~ Description for leather funnel
#. ~ Description for birchbark funnel
#. ~ Description for makeshift funnel
#. ~ Description for funnel
#. ~ Description for metal funnel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A funnel that will collect rainwater into the tank beneath it."
msgstr ""
"Es un embudo que recolectará agua de lluvia en el tanque que tiene abajo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "scoop"
msgstr "pala mecánica"

#. ~ Description for scoop
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A scoop.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it"
" will scoop up any loose items that it travels over, putting them into the "
"vehicle's storage."
msgstr ""
"Es una pala. Usá los controles del vehículo para activarla o desactivarla. "
"Cuando está activada, recogerá todos los objetos sueltos por los que pase, y"
" los pondrá en el almacenamiento del vehículo."

#. ~ Description for water purifier
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A water purifier, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  You can use it to "
"purify water in a container or in the vehicle's tanks.  'e'xamine the tile "
"with the purifier to use it."
msgstr ""
"Es un purificador de agua alimentado por las baterías del vehículo. Lo podés"
" usar para potabilizar agua en un recipiente o en los tanques del vehículo. "
"Usá 'e' para examinar el espacio donde está ubicado el purificador."

#. ~ Description for plow
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A plow.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it "
"will create a furrow in any dirt it travels over, making it suitable for "
"planting seeds.  It should be placed in front of any seed drills on the "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es un arado. Usá los controles del vehículo para activarlo o desactivarlo. "
"Cuando está activado, creará un surco en la tierra por la que pase, "
"haciéndola adecuada para plantar semillas. Debería ser ubicado adelante de "
"la sembradora que tenga el vehículo."

#. ~ Description for seed drill
#. ~ Description for advanced seed drill
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A seed drill.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  You can load "
"it with seeds by examining it.  When turned on, it will drop seeds as the "
"vehicle moves, or plant them in furrowed dirt.  It should be placed behind "
"any plows on the vehicle, and any wheels should be placed so they won't run "
"over the plants."
msgstr ""
"Es una sembradora. Usá los controles del vehículo para activarla o "
"desactivarla. Podés examinarla para cargarla con semillas. Cuando está "
"activa, dejará caer las semillas a medida que el vehículo avanza, o las "
"plantará en tierra arada. Debería estar ubicado atrás del arado, y las "
"ruedas deben estar puestas de manera que no pasen por encima de las plantas."

#. ~ Description for reaper
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"on, it will cut down plants that it travels over.  It should be placed in "
"front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient operation.  It does not "
"include cargo space of its own so you need install a cargo space of some "
"kind elsewhere in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una cosechadora automática. Usá los controles del vehículo para activarla"
" o desactivarla. Cuando está activada, cortará las plantas por las que pasa."
" Debería estar ubicada adelante del arado para una operación eficiente. No "
"incluye espacio de almacenamiento así que necesitás instalar algo en el "
"vehículo para juntar las plantas."

#. ~ Description for advanced reaper
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"on, it will cut down plants and store them in the vehicle's cargo.  It "
"should be placed in front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient "
"operation.  It has internal cargo space for collecting the harvest."
msgstr ""
"Es una cosechadora automática. Usá los controles del vehículo para activarla"
" o desactivarla. Cuando está activada, cortará las plantas y las pondrá en "
"el espacio de almacenamiento del vehículo. Debería estar ubicada adelante "
"del arado para una operación eficaz. Tiene un espacio de almacenamiento "
"interno para recolectar la cosecha."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cargo lock"
msgstr "bloqueo para puerta de carga"

#. ~ Description for cargo lock
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of locks.  Attached to a suitable cargo space, it will prevent other "
"people from accessing the cargo and taking your stuff."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de cerraduras. Unida a un espacio de carga, evitará que otras"
" personas puedan acceder a la carga y afanarte las cosas."

#. ~ Description for turret mount
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A rotating, universal mount for a weapon.  If your hands are empty, you can "
"stand on the same tile as a turret mount and 'f'ire the weapon."
msgstr ""
"Es una montura giratoria y universal para un arma. Si tus manos están "
"vacías, te podés parar en el mismo espacio de la torreta y disparar el arma "
"con 'f'."

#. ~ Description for turret control unit
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of motor, camera, and an AI unit which allows for tracking targets, "
"friend-or-foe identification, and firing the connected turret in full "
"automatic mode.  When installed over the turret, it will enable auto "
"targeting mode for said turret."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de motor, cámara y unidad de IA que permite rastrear "
"objetivos, identificación amigo-enemigo y disparar la torreta conectada en "
"modo automático completo. Cuando está instalada sobre la torreta, activará "
"el modo de autoselección de objetivo."

#. ~ Description for wooden wheel mount
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A piece of wood with holes suitable for a bike or motorbike wheel."
msgstr ""
"Es un pedazo de madera con agujeros adecuados para una rueda de bicicleta o "
"moto."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wooden wheel mount (steerable)"
msgstr "soporte de madera para ruedas (maniobrable)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "light wheel mount (steerable)"
msgstr "soporte liviano para ruedas (maniobrable)"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wheel hub assembly"
msgstr "buje"

#. ~ Description for wheel hub assembly
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Connection where wheels can be connected on.  This particular one is fit for"
" normal car wheels."
msgstr ""
"Es donde las ruedas se conectan. Este en particular es adecuado para ruedas "
"de auto normal."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wheel hub assembly (steerable)"
msgstr "buje (maniobrable)"

#. ~ Description for heavy wheel hub assembly
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"Connection where wheels can be connected on.  This particular one is fit for"
" large car wheels."
msgstr ""
"Es donde las ruedas se conectan. Este en particular es adecuado para ruedas "
"de auto grande."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "heavy wheel hub assembly (steerable)"
msgstr "buje grande (maniobrable)"

#. ~ Description for rail wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A strong metal wheel.  A flange helps keep it on a rail, but makes it "
"perform terribly when not on a rail."
msgstr ""
"Es una rueda fuerte de metal. Un reborde ayuda a mantenerla sobre la vía "
"pero causa que tenga un desempeño espantoso cuando no está en una vía."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "rail wheel (steerable)"
msgstr "rueda de ferrocarril (maniobrable)"

#. ~ Description for pair of small rail wheels
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A pair of small rail wheels.  It performs well when riding on a pair of "
"small rails.  It performs terribly when not on a rail.  Moreover, you can't "
"steer it."
msgstr ""
"Es un par de ruedas pequeñas de ferrocarril. Funcionan bien sobre un par de "
"pequeñas vías. Tienen un desempeño espantoso cuando no están sobre vías. Y "
"encima, no las podés maniobrar."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "roller drum"
msgstr "tambor de apisonadora"

#. ~ Description for wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A wheel."
msgstr "Es una rueda."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "racing slick"
msgstr "neumático liso de carrera"

#. ~ Description for armored wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A very strong, armored metal wheel."
msgstr "Es una rueda muy fuerte y blindada de metal."

#. ~ Description for wheelbarrow wheel
#. ~ Description for small wheel
#. ~ Description for unicycle wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A small wheel."
msgstr "Es una pequeña rueda."

#. ~ Description for bicycle wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A thin bicycle wheel."
msgstr "Es un rueda fina de bicicleta."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "casters"
msgstr "rueditas"

#. ~ Description for casters
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of small wheels, mounted on pivots, like the ones on a rolling office "
"chair or grocery cart."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de pequeñas ruedas, puesta en ejes, como las que usan las "
"sillas de oficina o los changuitos."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wheels"
msgstr "ruedas"

#. ~ Description for wheels
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A set of 10\" wheels with tough rubber tires."
msgstr "Es un conjunto de ruedas de 10\" con cubiertas resistentes de goma."

#. ~ Description for motorbike wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A small wheel from a motorcycle."
msgstr "Es una rueda chica de una moto."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "tricycle wheels"
msgstr "ruedas de triciclo"

#. ~ Description for tricycle wheels
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A set of three plastic wheels, with a larger one in the front, mounted with "
"bolts."
msgstr ""
"Es un conjunto de tres ruedas plásticas, una más grande que las otras "
"adelante, montadas con tornillos."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "unicycle wheel"
msgstr "rueda de monociclo"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wheelchair wheel"
msgstr "rueda de silla de ruedas"

#. ~ Description for wheelchair wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A pair of wheelchair wheels."
msgstr "Es un par de ruedas de silla de ruedas."

#. ~ Description for wide wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A wide wheel that provides more traction and better off-road performance."
msgstr ""
"Es una rueda ancha que brinda mayor tracción y mejor rendimiento todo "
"terreno."

#. ~ Description for wooden cart wheel
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A wooden wheel."
msgstr "Es una rueda de madera."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "windshield"
msgstr "parabrisas"

#. ~ Description for windshield
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "A sheet of glass that lets you see outside the vehicle."
msgstr "Es una lámina de vidrio que te permite ver hacia afuera del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "reinforced windshield"
msgstr "parabrisas reforzado"

#. ~ Description for reinforced windshield
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A sheet of glass that lets you see outside the vehicle.  Reinforced with "
"wire to make it harder to break than normal glass."
msgstr ""
"Es una lámina de vidrio que te permite ver hacia afuera del vehículo. "
"Reforzada con alambre para hacerla más resistente a las roturas que el "
"vidrio normal."

#. ~ Description for hauling space
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A huge, empty space used in truck trailers to transport vast quantities of "
"stuff."
msgstr ""
"Es un enorme espacio vacío utilizado por los semirremolques para transportar"
" vastas cantidades de cosas."

#. ~ Description for refrigerator
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A medium-sized household refrigerator, converted to utilize vehicle power.  "
"When turned on, food inside will be cooled, extending the time it has before"
" spoiling."
msgstr ""
"Es una heladera mediana de hogar, convertida para utilizar la energía de un "
"vehículo. Cuando está encendida, la comida adentro estará refrigerada "
"extendiendo su vida útil."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "freezer"
msgstr "freezer"

#. ~ Description for freezer
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A household fridge, converted to run at a much lower temperature and on "
"vehicle power.  When turned on, food inside will be frozen, completely "
"stopping it from spoiling."
msgstr ""
"Es un freezer de hogar convertido para funcionar a mucha menor temperatura y"
" usar la alimentación de un vehículo. Cuando está encendido, la comida "
"adentro se congelará, frenando completamente su deterioro."

#. ~ Description for MetalMaster forge buddy
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A welding and metalworking station, powered by the vehicle's battery.  "
"'e'xamine the forge rig to utilize its welder or soldering iron; you'll "
"still need glare protection."
msgstr ""
"Es una estación de soldadura y herrería, alimentada por la batería del "
"vehículo. Apretá 'e' para examinar la forja y utilizar su soldadora; vas a "
"necesitar protección para los ojos."

#. ~ Description for cooking rig
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An all-in-one kitchen unit and chemistry lab.  'e'xamine it to use its "
"hotplate to heat up food or drinks."
msgstr ""
"Es una unidad de cocina y un laboratorio de química, todo en uno. Apretá 'e'"
" para examinarla y usar su anafe eléctrico para calentar comidas y bebidas."

#. ~ Description for KitchenMaster cooking buddy
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An all-in-one kitchen unit, chemistry lab, and food preparation area.  "
"'e'xamine it to use its hotplate to heat up food or drinks."
msgstr ""
"Es una unidad de cocina, un laboratorio de química y un área de preparación "
"de comida, todo en uno. Apretá 'e' para examinarla y usar su anafe eléctrico"
" para calentar comidas y bebidas."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cargo trough"
msgstr "tolva de carga"

#. ~ Description for cargo trough
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"This is little more than a sheetmetal basin welded to the bottom of the "
"vehicle, extending below it.  Though it holds a lot of stuff, its shoddiness"
" makes it fragile."
msgstr ""
"Es poco más que un bol de metal soldado en su parte de abajo a un vehículo, "
"extendiéndose por debajo. Aunque puede contener muchas cosas, es un poco "
"frágil."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Gibson S86"
msgstr ""

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted Accipiter Hawk-00"
msgstr ""

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "crude plating"
msgstr "placa rudimentaria"

#. ~ Description for crude plating
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A piece of sheet metal welded onto a vehicle as armor.  Thin, and not as "
"protective as proper armor, but it'll do if there's nothing else available."
msgstr ""
"Es un pedazo de lámina de metal soldada al vehículo para protegerlo. Delgada"
" y no tan protectora como un blindado apropiado pero sirve si no tenés otra "
"cosa."

#. ~ Description for control station
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A large and complex dashboard mounted with steering controls and several LCD"
" touch screens for controlling vehicle systems."
msgstr ""
"Es un tablero de control largo y complejo montado con controles de dirección"
" y varias pantallas táctiles LCD para controlar los sistemas del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "mounted external tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado (200L)"

#. ~ Description for ultralight frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ultralight titanium framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted "
"on it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's "
"size."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura ultraligera de titanio. Se pueden poner otras partes del "
"vehículo en ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para incrementar el "
"tamaño del vehículo."

#. ~ Description for ultralight foldable frame
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"An ultralight titanium foldable framework.  Other vehicle components can be "
"mounted on it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the "
"vehicle's size."
msgstr ""
"Es una estructura plegable ultraligera de titanio. Se pueden poner otras "
"partes del vehículo en ella, y puede ser unida a otras estructuras para "
"incrementar el tamaño del vehículo."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "robot_carrier"
msgstr "cargador_robot"

#. ~ Description for robot_carrier
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A cargo space for carrying robots.  'e'xamine it to capture a robot next to "
"you, or to release the robot currently contained.  When selecting a robot to"
" capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the part."
msgstr ""
"Es un espacio de carga para llevar robots. Usá 'e' para examinar y capturar "
"un robot cercano, o para liberar al robot que esté adentro. Cuando "
"selecciones el robot para capturar, seleccioná el espacio en el que está en "
"relación a vos, no a la parte."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A closed cycle, external combustion steam turbine.  Burns coal from a bunker"
" in the vehicle to produce steam."
msgstr ""
"Es una turbina de vapor de combustión externa, con ciclo cerrado. Quema "
"carbón de la carbonera del vehículo para producir vapor."

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "cargo shelving"
msgstr "estanterías de carga"

#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid "wiring"
msgstr "cableado"

#. ~ Description for wiring
#: lang/json/vehicle_part_from_json.py
msgid ""
"A length of heavy duty copper wire, useful for routing power from one part "
"of a vehicle to another part."
msgstr ""
"Es un pedazo de cable de cobre resistente, útil para conducir energía de una"
" parte del vehículo a otra."

